# Line endings, decided once instead of per clone.
#
# Every text blob in this repo is LF, but a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true gets a CRLF working tree -- which makes the dashboard's
# `npm run format:check` (prettier, endOfLine=lf) report ~1000 files that are
# fine in git and fine on Linux. Pinning eol=lf here means the check says the
# same thing on every machine.
* text=auto
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.less text eol=lf
*.scss text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
